<title>USA: George Mason Q2 aided by interest income.</title>
<headline>George Mason Q2 aided by interest income.</headline>
<dateline>CHANTILLY, Va. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>George Mason Bankshares Inc said on Wednesday that its second quarter earnings were aided by an increase in net interest income to $7.9 million from $6.4 million.</p>
<p>The company's net loans increased to $409.3 million as of June 30, 1997 from $326.6 million a year ago, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company said it has expanded its market share in Virginia, Maryland and Washington D.C.</p>
